ns H1-H10, the null feature_041 contrast H12, the failed feature_031 validation H11, and the null, small, imprecise, opposite, or below-threshold contrasts in the H14-H24 screen, including H18 which is direction-supported but below the 0.15 point-estimate threshold. Unresolved uncertainty remains because the second-wave marginal screen H25-H36 is still untested, the predictors have opaque labels and no assigned biology, and the H21 interval still leaves slight uncertainty near the threshold boundary. The most informative next analysis is to run the already registered second-wave main-effect screen H25-H36, then use those results to decide whether to follow up accepted predictors with motivated subgroup or interaction tests, starting with the largest accepted effects rather than returning to the already null marker family."
