  "narrative": "All due estimates are signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For negative-direction feature_063, feature_037, and feature_027 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a lower outcome_001 value, i.e. stronger composite dependency; for positive-direction feature_002 and feature_010 claims, a positive signed estimate means a higher outcome_001 value, i.e. weaker dependency.\n\nH135 tests feature_063 in a relatively clean joint context defined by feature_002=0, feature_037=0, feature_010=0, and feature_027=0. The signed estimate is +0.260 [0.182, 0.338], with valid cell sizes (122 exposed, 839 comparator). The entire interval lies above the 0.15-unit threshold and in the claimed direction. This supports a dataset-specific conditional association between feature_063=1 and stronger composite dependency even when the other major binary associations are set aside. It is not an independence or causal statement; it is a conditional mean difference in this supplied dataset.\n\nH136 tests feature_063 within feature_027=0. The signed estimate is +0.235 [0.138, 0.331]. The point estimate exceeds the threshold and the interval excludes zero, although the lower bound is slightly below 0.15. Given that feature_063 has been accepted overall and in several validated or stable contexts, and that feature_027=0 comprises most of the dataset, I accept this as supporting the same feature_063 association outside the very strong low-prevalence feature_027 context. The exact magnitude in this particular context remains somewhat less precise than in H135, but there is no evidence against the accepted pattern.\n\nThe feature_038-context pair is the most scientifically informative new result. H137, feature_063 within feature_038 >= 0, is strongly positive: +0.529 [0.395, 0.664], with the lower bound far above threshold. H138, feature_063 within feature_038 <= 0, is essentially null and opposite to the claimed direction: -0.029 [-0.138, 0.079]. This contrast suggests that the feature_063 association may be concentrated in the positive feature_038 assay context, but these are separate subgroup mean differences rather than an explicit interaction test. Confounding or co-occurrence with feature_038, overlap at the exact zero cut point, or multiplicity across many context analyses could contribute to the apparent heterogeneity. I therefore accept H137 and reject H138, but I propose a formal feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction to determine whether the difference between contexts itself exceeds the threshold and has acceptable uncertainty. I avoid interpreting H137/H138 as proven effect modification.\n\nThe feature_037 checks show large, consistent stronger-dependency associations in both feature_038 halves: H139 +0.864 [0.773, 0.956] and H140 +0.779 [0.689, 0.869]. Both lower bounds far exceed 0.15. These are simple conditional persistence checks, not evidence of independence from feature_038 or effect modification.\n\nH141 and H142 test feature_002 across feature_018 halves and show large, consistent positive effects: +0.879 [0.786, 0.972] and +0.788 [0.696, 0.880]. H143 and H144 test feature_010 across feature_036 halves: +0.455 [0.310, 0.599] and +0.391 [0.262, 0.521]. In each case the interval lies entirely above the threshold and in the claimed direction. These support dataset-specific persistence of the accepted feature_002 and feature_010 associations across the tested standardized-assay contexts, without implying causality, mechanistic explanation, or generalizability.\n\nH145 and H146 test feature_027 across feature_038 halves. Despite low exposed prevalence, cell sizes are adequate: 51 and 79 exposed. The estimates are +0.859 [0.690, 1.027] and +0.794 [0.643, 0.944], both with lower bounds far above threshold. This supports the robust dataset-specific feature_027 stronger-dependency association in both feature_038 contexts, although inference remains observational and label-opaque.\n\nOverall, all intervals have plausible Welch independence assumptions and meet the 20-observation cell rule. The main limitations are multiplicity, post-hoc context selection around already accepted core predictors, overlap among contexts, and the inability to adjust for confounders using the requested unadjusted conditional mean comparisons. No causal, mechanistic, biological-role, or effect-modification claims are supported. No validation is requested because no new voluntary validation requests remain; the new feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction is the highest-value next analysis.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 appraise: H135-H146 delivered. Accepted H135 (clean joint-context feature_063, +0.260 [0.182, 0.338]) and H136 (feature_063 within feature_027=0, +0.235 [0.138, 0.331]; point above threshold, lower just below, but consistent with accepted overall feature_063). Accepted H137 (feature_063 within feature_038>=0, +0.529 [0.395, 0.664]) and rejected H138 (feature_063 within feature_038<=0, -0.029 [-0.138, 0.079]). This suggests possible concentration of feature_063 effect in positive feature_038 context, but no formal interaction has been tested. Proposed a new feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction (subgroup feature_038>=0, direction -1) as parented to H137, motivated by R143/R144.\n\nAccepted persistence contexts: feature_037 in feature_038 halves H139/H140; feature_002 in feature_018 halves H141/H142; feature_010 in feature_036 halves H143/H144; feature_027 in feature_038 halves H145/H146. All intervals clear the 0.15 threshold and support dataset-specific conditional mean differences. These are not independent replications, independence claims, interaction tests, causal effects, or generalizable claims.\n\nNo validation budget remains. Next analysis priorities: (1) newly proposed feature_063 x feature_038 interaction to formally assess context heterogeneity; (2) existing H147 feature_046 level_003 vs level_001 if capacity permits; (3) lower-priority pending items H91, H97, H114, H122 remain deferred/lower priority unless they become analytically useful. Core dataset-specific picture remains: feature_037=1 and feature_027=1 associated with much stronger dependency; feature_063=1 associated with stronger dependency overall and in many contexts, possibly feature_038-dependent; feature_002=1 and feature_010=1 associated with weaker dependency in this outcome orientation. All biological interpretation remains uncertain."
