  "narrative": "Current synthesis report.\n\nDue assessment: H115 tested feature_063=1 versus feature_063=0 among observations with feature_040 <= -7, in the direction indicating stronger composite dependency. Returned estimates are already signed to that direction, so a positive value means feature_063=1 is associated with a lower outcome_001 value, i.e. stronger dependency. Discovery R120 was +0.1528 [0.0262, 0.2793], with cell sizes 138 and 952. The newly released independent validation R127 is stronger: +0.3748 [0.1977, 0.5519], with cell sizes 138 and 953, and its lower bound is above the 0.15 composite dependency-score-unit threshold even under the stringent independent alpha. I therefore accept H115 and close it. This supports a dataset-specific conditional association between feature_063=1 and stronger composite dependency in the low feature_040 band. It is a simple within-band mean difference, not an interaction test, causal effect, mechanistic claim, or generalizability claim.\n\nSupported core findings in this supplied dataset: feature_037=1 is associated with markedly stronger composite dependency; the accepted negative-direction estimate was approximately +0.833 in discovery and +0.831 in independent validation. feature_027=1 is associated with much stronger dependency despite low prevalence; the accepted overall estimate was +0.792 in discovery and +0.768 in independent validation, and it remains large in many named conditional contexts. feature_063=1 is associated with stronger dependency overall and in many contexts; the clean joint context with feature_002=0, feature_037=0, feature_010=0, and feature_027=0 gave +0.260 [0.182, 0.338], and the low feature_040 band is now independently validated. feature_002=1 is associated with weaker dependency, with accepted/validated positive-direction estimates around +0.83 in discovery and +0.78 in validation. feature_010=1 is also associated with weaker dependency, with validated positive-direction estimates around +0.42 in discovery and +0.38 in validation. These are dataset-specific associations on the composite outcome, not biological roles or causal effects.\n\nImportant negative or unsupported findings remain important: the constructed binary markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 do not show meaningful main-effect differences or supported interactions; feature_031 and feature_006 do not survive validation; many categorical contrasts are null; and all explicitly tested interactions among the core binary predictors so far are unsupported. Thus accepted within-context estimates should not be read as evidence of effect modification, independence from the conditioning variables, or biological mechanism.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty: the apparent concentration of the feature_063 association in the positive feature_038 context is suggestive because H137 was strong (+0.529 [0.395, 0.664]) while H138 in feature_038 <= 0 was null (-0.029 [-0.138, 0.079]), but this is not yet a formal interaction; H148 is the most informative next analysis. The middle feature_040 band for feature_063 remains unsupported even though both broad <= -7 and extreme <= -9 bands are accepted, so no localized band-interaction or dose-response conclusion is justified. Small or imprecise contexts such as H91 and H97 remain unresolved with low priority, and pending analyses H114, H122, H147, and H148 may be useful if analysis capacity allows. Independent validation budget is exhausted, so remaining conclusions must rest on the accumulated discovery and validation evidence in this dataset.",
