cy (validated approximately +0.768); feature_002=1 is associated with weaker dependency (validated approximately +0.781); feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency (validated approximately +0.378); and feature_063=1 is associated with stronger dependency overall and in several contexts, including validated low feature_040 bands and a formally accepted interaction showing concentration in the feature_038 >= 0 context. Important negative findings include null or rejected main effects and interactions for the constructed markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015; rejected feature_046 contrasts tested so far; rejected interactions among core binary predictors apart from feature_063-by-feature_038>=0; and rejected or unsupported feature_063 effects in some contexts such as feature_038 <= 0, feature_018 >= 0, and the middle feature_040 band. Unresolved items include the weak feature_063 signal in feature_036 >= 0 (H154), pending decomposition of the positive feature_038 context by feature_037, feature_018, and feature_036, and whether the feature_063-feature_038 interaction persists or disappears inside the low feature_040 band. The most informative next analyses are the registered feature_063 context tests H160-H167, plus the two new proposals here: a direct feature_063 mean difference within feature_038 >= 0 and feature_040 <= -7, and an interaction of feature_063 by feature_038 >= 0 restricted to the low feature_040 band. These will help determine whether the accepted feature_038 interaction is robust, confounded or confounded-with feature_040, or context-specific. All conclusions remain observational dataset-specific associations with opaque predictor labels; they do not establish causality, independence from unmeasured factors, biological mechanism, or generalizability.",
