  "narrative": "Final synthesis at iteration 18/25. No validation results or response deadlines were supplied, and independent validation requests are exhausted, so I make no validation-driven accept/reject changes. I closed remaining deferred unresolved investigations without changing their scientific status.\n\nSign convention: outcome_001 is more negative when dependency is stronger. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has lower outcome_001, i.e. stronger dependency. For accepted direction +1 claims for feature_002 and feature_010, positive signed estimates mean higher outcome_001, i.e. weaker dependency. Thresholds are absolute 0.15 outcome_001 units.\n\nSupported dataset-specific core associations. feature_037=1 is robustly associated with stronger dependency: signed +0.833 (R14; 95% CI 0.767 to 0.898), independently validated at +0.831 (R39; CI 0.740 to 0.922). feature_027=1 is robustly associated with stronger dependency: signed +0.792 (R103; CI 0.676 to 0.907), validated at +0.768 (R115; CI 0.611 to 0.926). feature_002=1 is robustly associated with weaker dependency: signed +0.832 (R16; CI 0.766 to 0.897), validated at +0.781 (R78; CI 0.692 to 0.869). feature_010=1 is robustly associated with weaker dependency: signed +0.423 (R17; CI 0.327 to 0.520), validated at +0.378 (R65; CI 0.247 to 0.510). These four are the most defensible outcome_001 associations in this dataset. They also persist across many strata, including feature_019, feature_012, feature_040, feature_065>=50, feature_038, feature_018, and feature_036 bands, and among core-zero subpopulations (e.g. R61/R62, R46/R47, R68/R69, R106-R111, R155-R158). These are not artifacts of the other tested core binary markers within this supplied dataset, but residual confounding remains possible.\n\nfeature_063: the scientifically informative result is context dependence, not a precise broad main effect. The overall feature_063 contrast has accepted direction toward stronger dependency but uncertain magnitude near the threshold: signed +0.227 (R22; CI 0.131 to 0.323) with validation +0.276 (R26; CI 0.130 to 0.421). Both intervals include values below 0.15, so the exact overall magnitude remains unresolved. The robust feature is that feature_063 effects are concentrated when feature_038 is nonnegative/high. Direct feature_063 contrasts are accepted and meaningful in feature_038>=0, >=0.5, and >=1 bands (R143 +0.529 CI 0.395 to 0.664; R190 +0.501 CI 0.333 to 0.670; R189 +0.514 CI 0.267 to 0.761), and accepted feature_063-by-feature_038 interactions quantify this localization (R153 +0.559 CI 0.387 to 0.731; R193 +0.399 CI 0.200 to 0.598; R165 +0.338 CI 0.072 to 0.604). Low/nonpositive feature_038 negative controls are null or subthreshold (e.g. R144, R188, R222, R223), so a feature_038-negative context does not support the same feature_063 association. Core-zero restrictions further support persistence: R187 +0.568 CI 0.466 to 0.669 and R218 +0.777 CI 0.699 to 0.854.\n\nfeature_018 modifies the feature_063 association by attenuation as feature_018 becomes nonnegative. Accepted attenuation interactions include R170 +0.456 CI 0.266 to 0.646 overall; R194 +0.744 CI 0.451 to 1.036 within feature_038>=0; R205 +0.706 CI 0.357 to 1.054 within feature_038>=0.5; and R221 +0.686 CI 0.322 to 1.049 within feature_038>=0.5 using the feature_018>=0.25 cutoff. The corresponding residual direct effects for nonnegative or high feature_018 are absent or below threshold: R192 +0.126 CI -0.160 to 0.413 in feature_038>=0.5 with feature_018>=0; R195 +0.022 CI -0.231 to 0.274 in feature_038>=0 with feature_018>=0.5; R220 +0.087 CI -0.224 to 0.398 in feature_038>=0.5 with feature_018>=0.25. Strong direct effects persist when feature_018 is low: R191 +0.832 CI 0.626 to 1.038 in feature_038>=0.5 with feature_018<=0; R201 +0.734 CI 0.548 to 0.921 with feature_018<=0.5; R216 +0.701 CI 0.426 to 0.976 with feature_018<=-0.5; R224 +0.622 CI 0.357 to 0.888 in feature_038 0.5 to 1.0 with feature_018<=0.5. R196 +0.560 CI 0.269 to 0.851 suggests residual effect in feature_038>=0 with feature_018 between 0 and 0.5, but the cell is small (20 exposed, 153 comparator), so this boundary is accepted as a dataset-specific signal rather than a stable biological threshold.\n\nfeature_036 does not provide established independent localization or attenuation of feature_063. In high feature_038, direct feature_063 contrasts remain meaningful for both feature_036 signs (R206 +0.516 CI 0.298 to 0.733 for feature_036<=0 and R207 +0.487 CI 0.217 to 0.756 for feature_036>=0), while the corresponding feature_036 interactions are null or below threshold (R217 +0.029 CI -0.313 to 0.371 within feature_038>=0.5; R171 +0.137 CI -0.055 to 0.330 overall). The overall direct feature_036>=0 estimate is borderline only (R159 +0.160 CI 0.025 to 0.296), and I keep it unresolved. feature_040 is secondary: feature_063 effects can persist in low feature_040 bands, including R120 +0.153 CI 0.026 to 0.279 with validation R127 +0.375 CI 0.198 to 0.552, and feature_063 effects combined with feature_038>=0 are accepted in feature_040-restricted subsets (e.g. R172, R173, R174). However feature_040-only feature_063 interactions are inconsistent or imprecise, so feature_040 should not be prioritized as a primary context factor.\n\nNegative findings are broad and informative. Constructed markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 show no main or interaction effect above threshold (H1-H10). feature_031 produced a below-threshold near-positive discovery signal that failed independent validation (R11 discovery, R13 validation). feature_041, feature_023, feature_048, feature_001, feature_035, feature_011, feature_006, feature_014, feature_021, feature_047, feature_017, feature_060, feature_022, feature_013, feature_033, feature_050, and most tested categorical contrasts (e.g. feature_024, feature_046, feature_059, feature_061, feature_034, feature_062, feature_052, feature_054) are not supported at the 0.15 threshold. Most tested interactions among core binary predictors, including feature_002 by feature_010, feature_037 by feature_002 or feature_010, and feature_063 within feature_037=1 or feature_010=1, are null or below threshold. Low feature_038 feature_063 controls are null. feature_036 is not an independent modifier. These are dataset-specific negative results; they do not rule out effects untested, effects in different strata, effects below this threshold, or causal effects.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. The main open scientific boundary questions are exact feature_038 thresholds (0 versus 0.5 versus 1) and exact feature_018 attenuation onset (likely somewhere between 0 and 0.5, with 0.25 tested and cells small). R213 and R215 are invalid due insufficient cell size, and R214 is unresolved because the lower confidence bound is below threshold and the exposed cell is small, so intermediate feature_038/feature_018 bands cannot be further localized reliably in this dataset with remaining capacity. The exact overall feature_063 magnitude remains uncertain because both discovery and validation intervals cross 0.15. Whether feature_036 has any independent role remains uncertain because it appears correlated with feature_038 context and the direct feature_036>=0 estimate is borderline. feature_040 is secondary and possibly collinear with other predictors. General sources of uncertainty include observational confounding, correlated predictors, informative missingness for feature_065, arbitrary categorical/standardized thresholds, multiplicity, small cells, and absence of independent validation for the feature_038/feature_018 feature_063 context model. No causal, mechanistic, biological-role, adjustment-adequacy, or generalizability claim is supported by this composite endpoint and opaque labels.\n\nMost informative next analysis. The next best scientific step is not another arbitrary threshold split. If independent data are available,